NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000148 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000149 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000150 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000151 "CPAN::Common::Index - Common library for searching CPAN modules, authors and distributions"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000152 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000153 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000154 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000155 "version 0.010"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000156 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000157 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000158 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000159 "    use CPAN::Common::Index::Mux::Ordered;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000160 "    use Data::Dumper;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000161 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000162 "    $index = CPAN::Common::Index::Mux::Ordered->assemble("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000163 "        MetaDB => {},"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000164 "        Mirror => { mirror => \"http://cpan.cpantesters.org\" },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000165 "    );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000166 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000167 "    $result = $index->search_packages( { package => \"Moose\" } );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000168 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000169 "    print Dumper($result);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000170 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000171 "    # {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000172 "    #   package => 'MOOSE',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000173 "    #   version => '2.0802',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000174 "    #   uri     => \"cpan:///distfile/ETHER/Moose-2.0802.tar.gz\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000175 "    # }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000176 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000177 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000178 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000179 "This module provides a common library for working with a variety of CPAN index"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000180 "services.  It is intentionally minimalist, trying to use as few non-core"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000181 "modules as possible."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000182 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000183 "The C<CPAN::Common::Index> module is an abstract base class that defines a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000184 "common API.  Individual backends deliver the API for a particular index."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000185 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000186 "As shown in the SYNOPSIS, one interesting application is multiplexing -- using"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000187 "different index backends, querying each in turn, and returning the first"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000188 "result."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000189 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000190 "=head1 METHODS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000191 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000192 "=head2 search_packages (ABSTRACT)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000193 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000194 "    $result = $index->search_packages( { package => \"Moose\" });"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000195 "    @result = $index->search_packages( \\%advanced_query );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000196 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000197 "Searches the index for a package such as listed in the CPAN"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000198 "F<02packages.details.txt> file.  The query must be provided as a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000199 "reference.  Valid keys are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000200 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000201 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000202 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000203 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000204 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000205 "package -- a string, regular expression or code reference"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000206 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000207 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000208 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000209 "version -- a version number or code reference"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000210 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000211 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000212 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000213 "dist -- a string, regular expression or code reference"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000214 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000215 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000216 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000217 "If the query term is a string or version number, the query will be for an exact"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000218 "match.  If a code reference, the code will be called with the value of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000219 "field for each potential match.  It should return true if it matches."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000220 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000221 "Not all backends will implement support for all fields or all types of queries."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000222 "If it does not implement either, it should \"decline\" the query with an empty"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000223 "return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000224 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000225 "The return should be context aware, returning either a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000226 "single result or a list of results."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000227 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000228 "The result must be formed as follows:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000229 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000230 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000231 "      package => 'MOOSE',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000232 "      version => '2.0802',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000233 "      uri     => \"cpan:///distfile/ETHER/Moose-2.0802.tar.gz\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000234 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000235 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000236 "The C<uri> field should be a valid URI.  It may be a L<URI::cpan> or any other"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000237 "URI.  (It is up to a client to do something useful with any given URI scheme.)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000238 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000239 "=head2 search_authors (ABSTRACT)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000240 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000241 "    $result = $index->search_authors( { id => \"DAGOLDEN\" });"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000242 "    @result = $index->search_authors( \\%advanced_query );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000243 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000244 "Searches the index for author data such as from the CPAN F<01mailrc.txt> file."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000245 "The query must be provided as a hash reference.  Valid keys are"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000246 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000247 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000248 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000249 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000250 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000251 "id -- a string, regular expression or code reference"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000252 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000253 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000254 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000255 "fullname -- a string, regular expression or code reference"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000256 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000257 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000258 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000259 "email -- a string, regular expression or code reference"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000260 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000261 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000262 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000263 "If the query term is a string, the query will be for an exact match.  If a code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000264 "reference, the code will be called with the value of the field for each"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000265 "potential match.  It should return true if it matches."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000266 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000267 "Not all backends will implement support for all fields or all types of queries."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000268 "If it does not implement either, it should \"decline\" the query with an empty"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000269 "return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000270 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000271 "The return should be context aware, returning either a single result or a list"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000272 "of results."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000273 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000274 "The result must be formed as follows:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000275 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000276 "    {"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000277 "        id       => 'DAGOLDEN',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000278 "        fullname => 'David Golden',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000279 "        email    => 'dagolden@cpan.org',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000280 "    }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000281 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000282 "The C<email> field may not reflect an actual email address.  The 01mailrc file"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000283 "on CPAN often shows \"CENSORED\" when email addresses are concealed."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000284 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000285 "=head2 index_age"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000286 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000287 "    $epoch = $index->index_age;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000288 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000289 "Returns the modification time of the index in epoch seconds.  This may not make sense"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000290 "for some backends.  By default it returns the current time."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000291 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000292 "=head2 refresh_index"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000293 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000294 "    $index->refresh_index;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000295 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000296 "This ensures the index source is up to date.  For example, a remote"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000297 "mirror file would be re-downloaded.  By default, it does nothing."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000298 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000299 "=head2 attributes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000300 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000301 "Return attributes and default values as a hash reference.  By default"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000302 "returns an empty hash reference."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000303 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000304 "=head2 validate_attributes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000305 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000306 "    $self->validate_attributes;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000307 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000308 "This is called by the constructor to validate any arguments.  Subclasses"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000309 "should override the default one to perform validation.  It should not be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000310 "called by application code.  By default, it does nothing."
